About the copyright holder

Daniel García (cr0hn) is a cybersecurity researcher, developer, and trainer with
more than twenty years in the field. He started in ethical hacking (including
Telefónica R&D), later led API security work at 42Crunch, and focuses on
critical security, REST APIs, and systems that have to hold up under real load.

He has published 100+ open source security tools. Several shipped in Kali Linux
and BlackArch (among them Dockerscan, FestIn, Enteletaor, and Dockerfile
Security). He speaks at conferences, founded the Navaja Negra security
conference, and helped start the OWASP Madrid chapter. He also designs and
delivers hands-on secure-development workshops for engineering teams.

ByteBazaar (vulnerable-python) is part of that teaching line: a real Flask shop with
real bugs, released under MIT so developers can break it safely on their laptop.

- Website: https://cr0hn.com
- GitHub:  https://github.com/cr0hn
- Talks:   https://cr0hn.com/en/talks/
- Tools:   https://cr0hn.com/en/projects/
- Authors: see AUTHORS.md in this repository
